acquire-session-backup-locks

Lane: backend

Unit: backup-sessions-with-native-locks

ChildPatch: acquire-session-backup-locks

Form: GitDiff

Segment: none

Purpose: Provide a separate local session backup command that refuses every busy native session-data lock and archives a consistent zstd session snapshot.

Requires: Unit:normalization/normalize-base-roots-for-processes, Unit:normalization/route-thread-writer-locks-to-harness, Unit:backend/rebuild-sqlite-history-from-paginated-rollouts

Provides: Nonblocking acquisition and recheck of maintenance, writer coordination, all per-thread files and the home-directory index lock; exact session archive publication with no overwrite and cancellation-safe cleanup.

Boundary: Rollout production, migration, compression and index semantics remain with their native owners; the command never backs up SQLite or waits for active sessions.

Verification: rollout writer_lock tests cover every busy lock, partial release, name updates and fork-reference publication; CLI backup fixtures cover exact members, roundtrip bytes, no-clobber, missing sources and cancellation.


